1795387043559352	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.unlink	bn-3bh	{"target":"bn-g2i"}	blake3:2ipPMD_4LFJM6ou_NCVxChCH7DJ4e3WZsEwPyVHnJco
1795387043581154	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3jd	{"description":"# Context\n`scourge engagement check` is an operator command, not on the agent's path. It finds engagement stanzas that cannot support an oracle before any lead exists, so the operator does not learn it from a failed verify run (plan §4.6).\n\n# Do\n- Print the effects first, in the form `verify --plan` uses. Then run each principal's identity probe, and each property's plant and remove, once.\n- Persist a run and request key before any effect (INV-12). Remove only objects whose creation the plant's response established (INV-40), with the rule from M1.5.2.3.\n- Name each stanza that cannot support an oracle: no field that can hold a canary, no remove route, or a plant whose response does not establish creation.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] F-51, first three cases: each unusable stanza is named, and the effects were printed before anything was sent.\n- [ ] On the development fixture's example engagement, `check` passes and leaves no object behind.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §4.6, §6.5; INV-12, INV-40; F-51.\n","kind":"task","labels":["m1","surface"],"parent":"bn-3bh","size":"m","title":"M1.11.1 `engagement check`: run each probe, plant and remove once, and name unusable stanzas"}	blake3:zoHYOTBqEYEXg34DSrPaUrvLtJZ3eOsfl9lti_jWlOc
1795387043604556	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-3jd	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-3s5"}	blake3:1Nc-y7gqB99moT6tYTZFia58gI14zS-jjFcUAqQT1Bg
