1795387043745696	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-3jd	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-27k"}	blake3:7IoNSy9U3WImWUJSEooF5DXCN40rpoMNDBduLMR7PVM
1795387043776108	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-28q	{"description":"# Context\nWriting the engagement is the largest setup cost. `scourge engagement draft` starts it from what the instrument has already captured (plan §4.6).\n\n# Do\n- `scourge engagement draft --from-teapot [--openapi FILE]` writes one property for each resource shape in Teapot's site map and parameter inventory, and in the API schema if one is given.\n- It sends no traffic and leaves `readers` and `writers` unset.\n- It does not read Teapot's authorization matrix or findings, so the draft says nothing about where a flaw might be.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] A network sink sees nothing during `draft`.\n- [ ] With Teapot findings and an authorization matrix present, the draft is byte-identical to one made without them.\n- [ ] A draft from Teapot's capture of the development fixture passes `engagement check` once the operator has set its rules.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §4.6; notes/plan.evaluation.md §2 (hint parity).\n","kind":"task","labels":["m1","surface"],"parent":"bn-3bh","size":"m","title":"M1.11.2 `engagement draft --from-teapot`: one property per resource shape, rules unset, no traffic"}	blake3:8uW94J9qRGeqgkgEzOAup6RPt0uF1Q_PV-tHiyrrKrQ
