1795489058010007	scourge-orca-2ij	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2ij	{"body":"scourge-orca-2ij: implementation committed at 2403c3216cab32f0a8037f533ce7b6906fd26e32 (parent main 5009a9b6ec79e881a3c34d59ad7454019eeb8485).\n\nChanged files: crates/scourge-core/src/request.rs (new normalization/binding), crates/scourge-core/src/store/003_request_keys.sql (new migration), crates/scourge-core/src/store/mod.rs (declare/reopen/find request, request_keys CRUD, run load, lead CAS, typed error codes), crates/scourge-core/src/store/request_tests.rs (new), crates/scourge-core/tests/request_input.rs (new), crates/scourge-core/src/store/tests.rs (schema whitelist + migration version), crates/scourge-core/src/lib.rs (module).\n\nSemantics: declare_request writes normalized scourge.request-input.v1 + run + steps + resolved selector snapshot in one Immediate transaction (audit operation request.accept, subject run id) before any effect boundary; reopen_request compares stored canonical bytes before re-resolving defaults/selectors and returns the original receipt with the current run state and writes nothing; find_request returns None for both unknown and foreign keys; reopen/declare return typed RequestNotFound (OBJECT_NOT_FOUND/3) for absent and out-of-scope keys alike and never create a run under an issued key; different input is typed IdempotencyKeyReused (4); lead revisions are compare-and-set returning typed RevisionConflict (4).\n\nTests: cargo test -p scourge-core --offline (23 lib + 15 contract + 9 request_input + 2 doc) pass; TMPDIR=/home/bob/src/scourge/.maw/cache/t CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<ws>/target CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true just check exit 0 (14 test-result-ok blocks). No network, target, credential or external effect; the effect boundary in tests is a local counter plus a simulated panic.\n\nNote for the reviewer: scripts/test-candidate-topology.py fails with AF_UNIX path-too-long when TMPDIR is a long workspace path (target/tmp); with the short TMPDIR above it passes. Pre-existing environment sensitivity, not this change."}	blake3:vxea1NWoclvvFqcsndBaLY7QrC8w6QJcBXXEdws76a0
1795489082055313	scourge-orca-2ij	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2ij	{"body":"scourge-orca-2ij: review requested. Seal cr-1ip1z5, exact HEAD 2403c3216cab32f0a8037f533ce7b6906fd26e32, range 5009a9b6ec79..2403c3216cab (1 commit), reviewer scourge-security, status open. Rite anchor 01M85QT7GN9FV2QB20GZ1KGP3D in #scourge (thread 01M85QT5C06VQK94HSMWJ3P9H6). Not merged, not closed, not pushed; workspace and claims retained. Remaining: reviewer disposition on cr-1ip1z5."}	blake3:auFQPe35IjJYyLIuBvCkiC-40EXRufZa42pkcUrnFQ0
1795489225496108	scourge-orca-20u	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-20u	{"body":"Review fixes complete and re-review requested. HEAD aeba76239636c0596cd6ab5cae686c409cc0fd3c (workspace bn-20u), base main 5009a9b, previous checkpoint 38fc80b; only .seal/reviews/cr-1n2ppx/events.jsonl is uncommitted (the review log, committed at merge). Fixes: th-5jiysb per-field treatment matching with round-level POR-04 and false requiring every primary canary absent from F0/F2/F3; th-16uz08 MultiGzDecoder for all members plus total_in single-stream check rejecting trailing zlib/raw-deflate bytes; th-33yc3s round-level after_owner_read; th-mocv1y only frozen F0<F1<F3 ordering; th-16acoz dead assignment removed and byte-substring semantics documented and asserted; th-3u51lj fixture-shaped one-member document wrapper decoded strictly; plus compiled decode-limit ceilings (16 MiB / 10000x) with boundary tests and closed typed codings. Validation: just check exit 0 (cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings, 189 workspace tests of which scourge-verify has 120: contract 10, decoding 40, outcomes 11, per_field 8, por_checks 15, reason_codes 15, saved_observations 14, scope 7, plus all python contract/fixture/tamper gates), run with TMPDIR=/home/bob/t after /tmp hit quota. Mutation probes: reverting each of the six fixes fails its new tests. Seal cr-1n2ppx retargeted to target aeba762/base 5009a9b with the block vote cleared, reviewers [scourge-security]; 7 open threads carry evidence replies (6 findings + 1 residual-risk/closure thread) and were left open for the reviewer. Rite re-review anchor 01M85QY4MJ8575WCQR5NZCHT4F (label review-response) on channel scourge. Bone stays doing; no self-approval, merge, push, close, workspace destroy or claim release; claims bone://scourge/bn-20u and workspace://scourge/bn-20u held. Next: scourge-security rereview on aeba762, then finish per edict once approved."}	blake3:aiXgJNS5mfc-fjDFYjFsfX7L1DIfd7DYb7QYm3PDfGk
