1795489794976119	scourge-orca-tnk	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-tnk	{"body":"Progress: implementation, tests and review request complete; awaiting the dedicated security review.\n\nHEAD 90a48e3ff2c03296c70c7bcf916e8e5864802bd2 on workspace bn-tnk (base f0341f6e408e). Committed, not pushed, not merged.\n\nChanged files\n- crates/scourge-core/src/template/mod.rs (new): exact scourge.claim-template.v1 shape plus the compiled web-authz/private-object-read registry, pure Templates::resolve/resolve_with, typed ResolveError -> frozen ErrorCode, and FrozenExperiment::freeze/from_canonical_bytes.\n- crates/scourge-core/src/template/tests.rs (new): 31 unit tests.\n- crates/scourge-core/src/lib.rs: pub mod template.\n- crates/scourge-core/src/declaration.rs: claim-template field names in the diagnostic whitelist; registered_ref is crate-visible for oracle reference validation.\n- crates/scourge-core/src/engagement.rs: Sealed for Property so the declared property's canonical bytes are hashed.\n\nBehaviour\n- Property slots resolve only from the declared property; any lead or --slot value for read/plant/remove is SLOT_CONFLICT (exit 2) before any effect. Supplier authority is the input channel, never a value the input claims.\n- Unknown/duplicate/cross-channel/ambiguous slots, undeclared property or principal, same principal, engagement revision or disallowed effect, and unsupported class are typed refusals with the frozen codes and exits.\n- Missing slots return Resolution::Incomplete with name, kind, permitted suppliers and reason (not_supplied, no_property_selected, property_fixes_nothing).\n- INV-37 stays generic through an inert OperationMethods projection: a template that declares read as a lead-supplied selector must resolve to GET or HEAD, else METHOD_REFUSED (exit 8); the shipped template's read slot is an operator-only property slot.\n- The experiment digest binds template id/version, engagement revision/digest, property label/resource/digest, every slot value/source/supplier/value digest, principal bindings (session, verifier session, groups, identity probe), oracle id/version/digest, decoder id/version/limits and the effect profile; it binds no canary and no nonce. Field-by-field sensitivity matrix plus canary/nonce stability and key-set tests.\n\nValidation run (TMPDIR set to a short workspace path because the host /tmp is full): cargo test -p scourge-core (74 tests), cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -D warnings, cargo fmt --check, cargo doc, and the full just check (exit 0).\n\nNo target effects, no network, no adapter, no credentials, no dispatch. No self-approval, no merge, no push, no claim release.\n\nRemaining: the dedicated scourge-security review of cr-ifws6e (anchor 01M85RFT26K44Y9AG8H6D5QHPX) and then the lead's merge decision."}	blake3:0Ig_r-iYa2pJ-emp1yoTztaejtfEETCNdKocCRTwyCU
1795490115576387	scourge-orca-20u	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-20u	{"body":"Completed at final synced HEAD 8293549a87ad02c03f601866dc7fc513e609bc48. Seal cr-1n2ppx approved exact target with zero open threads after exhaustive oracle/decoder and integration rereviews. scourge-verify 120 tests, core tests, dependency pins and full just check passed. Accepted residuals are recorded in th-1cq1dq and cannot produce a wrong exposure verdict. Handing workspace and review log to lead for local merge."}	blake3:E64UzJitQ15u9nEzHGltbnUFae_akvLfU10grGSR4bE
