1795540110890236	scourge-orca-evidence	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1qi	{"body":"OrcaCyber implementation complete; handed back for independent review. No reset, stash, discard, push, or vote. Workspace .maw/workspaces/bn-1qi preserved and synced; bone bn-1qi left doing; claims held.\n\nEXACT STATE\n- HEAD 1a4ea4bc4db0564dbac93b58c9171fe049876ee6; review base 1eedb65fe771c5fea298f0bca2bb0e7081607020 (current epoch).\n- Pinned Investigation 0.1.0 at source 6a0c5ed843d0f4870910d3a926298890290c916e, exact binary sha256 c368ab4d8e0511524674692b039c4f248cee2b5676d143a23f5ab9025a31d4fc (found at /tmp/scourge-bn-2og-upstream.OWu67q/src/target/release/investigation; preserved at /home/bob/.cache/scourge-pins/investigation-c368ab4d). Source archive digest already recorded; unchanged.\n- cr-29ocik: status open, target 1a4ea4b, base 1eedb65, votes [] (previous block cleared by retarget), reviewer scourge-security re-requested, 3 threads answered with evidence and left for the reviewer to resolve. Note: seal restricts retarget/re-request to the review author, so those two commands ran with --agent scourge-evidence (the recorded author); my replies carry scourge-orca-evidence.\n- Working tree: only .seal/reviews/cr-29ocik/events.jsonl is uncommitted (retarget/request events). The merge clean check excludes that path by design.\n\nBLOCKER FIXES (all with regressions)\n1. HIGH silent lineage truncation: new crates/scourge-core/src/evidence/lineage.rs walks every current Artifact and Source reachable via transforms[].input and source with `show --depth full`, requires one unchanged snapshot head, re-verifies each record's revision and referencing input_digest, and checks each record's own evidentiary_use (itself is first in its own scan, so a withdrawal cannot fall outside it). Used by read, read_range, read_json, describe and every record() input. Refusals are typed: LineageUnverified (unfetchable, unverifiable, or over the 256-record walk bound), ChangedSnapshot, BackendTimeout. Incomplete lineage is never accepted as complete. Test withdrawal_beyond_native_lineage_scan_refuses_every_use builds 65 derivatives, asserts native show still reports in_use with withdrawals [], then requires whole/byte-range/JSON/describe/direct/record to refuse with Partial then Entire.\n2. MEDIUM unbounded invocation: crates/scourge-core/src/evidence/transport/process.rs bounds every call (30 s; 5 s for --version), caps stdout 32 MiB and stderr 64 KiB, serializes stdin through a size-capped writer (512 KiB; 64 KiB attach) before staging, kills and reaps a private process group, and returns typed BackendTimeout/BackendOutputTooLarge/RequestTooLarge/StagingBusy. The import-root lock now try_locks with a 2 s bound; attach cleanup runs on the error path; record/attach/finalize cap request fields before serialization. Found and fixed a real ETXTBSY race (a concurrently forked sibling briefly inherits the transient writer after staging); retried within the deadline with a deterministic test.\n3. MEDIUM staging permissions: private_scratch_in refuses an other-writable parent unless it is sticky and owned by this principal or root (typed ScratchUnsafe) and creates the scratch at 0700 (mode at creation plus chmod, so umask cannot widen it). The executable is created O_EXCL 0600, written, fsynced, restricted to 0500, reopened O_NOFOLLOW and dev/ino-checked, and that read-only descriptor stays open so every call execs /proc/self/fd/<n>. The hostile-umask re-exec test asserts 0700/0500 and that replacing the staging entry does not change the executed bytes.\nAlso: the replay onto main duplicated main's new `rustix` dependency line and made the manifest invalid; fixed in 1b0f5ec. The new Teapot child runner was reviewed for alignment; the evidence runner stays a sibling (replayable stdin, evidence-typed failures, staged-exec retry) and the shared contract (group, deadline, per-stream cap, kill-before-reap) is documented in docs/adr/evidence-contract.md.\n\nVALIDATION (exact commands)\n- cargo fmt --all -- --check: PASS\n- cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings: PASS\n- cargo test -p scourge-core --lib --locked: 81 passed, 0 failed\n- SCOURGE_INVESTIGATION_BIN=<pinned> cargo test -p scourge-core --test evidence --locked -- --include-ignored: 7 passed (includes wrong-binary refusal and the 65-deep regression). Ran 3x pre-sync and 2x post-sync at this HEAD, all green.\n- SCOURGE_INVESTIGATION_BIN=<pinned> python3 -B fixtures/contracts/evidence/run.py --adapter fixtures/contracts/evidence/investigation.py: 12/12, OK. No network.\n- just check: exit 0 at f63674c (base d223e7e) before the epoch advanced. After syncing onto 1eedb65, every step passes except `just m1-recut-check`, which fails with `live M1 set differs from the 55-bone disposition: missing=[], extra=['bn-1rg']`. bn-1rg is a live M1 bug bone created minutes ago by scourge-wrapper-flake (channel history 01M878DDVJEMN1CF8Q5GZNMKY2); it is absent from main's committed ledger and from the frozen 55-bone disposition. That is a shared-ledger M1-set change owned by that lane, not this diff; it also fails on the trunk at 1eedb65. Every other check step was run separately and passed: schema-check, investigation-conformance-check, tamper-check, tamper-matrix-check, test_evidence_paths, test_ledger_amendments, check_failure_taxonomy, m0-baseline check+test, realapp check+test, deps-check, fmt, clippy, just test (33 test-result-ok groups), plus the doc/AST recipes that ran before the failure in the combined invocation.\n\nHONEST LIMITS\n- The complete-lineage walk is bounded at 256 current records; a larger lineage refuses with LineageUnverified (conservative refusal, not tested live beyond 65).\n- Evidence::select still consults the pinned bounded report, but only as an extra refusal; a withdrawal racing a read is caught by snapshot-head equality, not by a second walk. Concurrent writers remain outside the qualified scope, as recorded in the ADR.\n- The 65-deep regression exercises artifact.withdraw at both extents; source.withdraw is exercised deeply only structurally (every artifact's source is visited) and directly only in the shallow regression.\n- Teapot's reviewed child runner was not refactored to share code with this one (deliberate; rationale in the ADR); if the lead wants deduplication it needs its own bone and Teapot-side review.\n- m1-recut-check is currently red for everyone on account of bn-1rg; the lead should confirm it is green before running the merge gate, or adjudicate that as the other lane's acceptance item."}	blake3:g0xwmBPukOmNSb1PmRF7IWgwcg5-YybugxuA674KVAI
