1795541138352638	scourge-orca-evidence	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1qi	{"body":"Native-review transport blocker fixed and revalidated; bone stays doing, claims held, no reviewer requested, no vote.\n\nEXACT STATE\n- Workspace .maw/workspaces/bn-1qi HEAD 9c22b5aa7b3a98cf4ae4a22a387768c1dc3a16d3 (fix commit 44afbc0, review-log commit 9c22b5a) on base/current main ba3b75fe41943d2ebfae501c6b5441ac4dbb43ca. Main advanced past the review base 1eedb65 during this turn; the workspace was committed clean first and then synced onto ba3b75f with `maw ws sync bn-1qi` (9 commits replayed cleanly, sibling invariant verified), and every check below was re-run at the new base.\n- cr-29ocik retargeted to anchor 9c22b5a / base ba3b75f. Status open, votes [] (retarget clears the previous block), 4 open threads, all answered and left for the reviewer to resolve. No reviewer re-requested and no vote cast, per instruction.\n- Thread th-187q8s answered with exact evidence as th-187q8s.2 by scourge-orca-evidence.\n- Working tree: only .seal/reviews/cr-29ocik/events.jsonl uncommitted (the reply and retarget events written after the final commit; committing them would move HEAD past the retarget target). The merge clean check excludes that path. Nothing was reset, stashed, discarded, pushed, merged, closed, released or re-created.\n\nWHAT CHANGED (conservative; no bound, cap, kill/reap, staging, ETXTBSY, lineage or redaction guarantee weakened)\n1. crates/scourge-core/src/evidence/transport/process.rs: stderr is captured inside its existing 64 KiB cap instead of being drained with None, and `Output` carries it. `run` checks with waitid(WNOWAIT|WNOHANG|EXITED) whether the leader had already finished BEFORE it signals the private process group and only then reaps, so a status reached on a post-leader timeout or overflow is the backend's own and the runner's SIGKILL is never reported. Kill-before-reap and the WNOWAIT group-ID guarantee are unchanged.\n2. crates/scourge-core/src/evidence/mod.rs: new public `BackendStatus { Exited(i32), Signaled(i32) }`, `BackendFault { Terminated, Timeout, OutputTooLarge }`, and `BackendDiagnostic { status, fault, stderr_bytes, stderr_digest, stderr_excerpt }`. The excerpt is redacted to printable ASCII, whitespace-collapsed and capped at 200 characters; raw stderr, control bytes and terminal escapes are never exposed. `BackendTimeout` and `BackendOutputTooLarge` now carry the diagnostic; `BackendFailed { diagnostic }` is new.\n3. crates/scourge-core/src/evidence/transport.rs: `run` = `process::run` + pure `interpret`. A nonzero exit without a well-formed inv.response.v1 error envelope is `BackendFailed` with status and diagnostic instead of `Protocol`; exit 0 with a malformed body stays `Protocol`; a well-formed error envelope keeps its existing typed mapping; a nonzero exit with a receipt-shaped body is no longer accepted as success.\n4. docs/adr/evidence-contract.md records the diagnostic contract and the tested/unclaimed scope.\n\nREGRESSIONS (deterministic; assertions strengthened, none weakened)\nevidence::transport::tests: a_stderr_only_failure_is_a_typed_backend_failure (stderr-only exit 3 -> BackendFailed Exited(3), exact length/digest/excerpt, explicitly not Protocol), a_signalled_child_without_a_code_keeps_its_signal (SIGKILL -> Signaled(9)), a_malformed_reply_is_only_a_protocol_error_when_the_child_succeeded, a_protocol_error_envelope_keeps_its_typed_mapping, diagnostics_are_bounded_and_redacted (bytes 0..=255 + 4 KiB + escapes: exact len/digest, ASCII-only 200-cap excerpt, no ESC/BEL in Display).\nevidence::transport::process::tests: leader_status_survives_a_descendant_holding_an_inherited_pipe (leader exits 7, descendant holds both pipes to the deadline -> BackendTimeout Exited(7), returns <3 s, orphan marker absent), capture_overflow_keeps_a_status_observed_first (stdout 4096 cap and stderr 64 KiB cap -> BackendOutputTooLarge Exited(0)), unfinished_child_times_out_with_or_without_a_valid_reply (timeout before status -> status null), both_streams_are_bounded_and_drained, timeout_stops_group_members_with_inherited_pipes, a_completed_child_keeps_its_streams_for_the_caller, bounded_runs_release_every_captured_stream (self re-exec single-threaded, /proc/self/fd identical across 4 rounds of failing runs).\n\nVALIDATION at HEAD 9c22b5a / base ba3b75f (short TMPDIR=/tmp/scourge-check, CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true)\n- cargo fmt --all -- --check: PASS\n- cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked --offline -- -D warnings: PASS\n- cargo test -p scourge-core --lib --locked --offline: 124 passed, 0 failed (18 evidence::transport tests green 10x pre-sync and 5x post-sync)\n- SCOURGE_INVESTIGATION_BIN=/home/bob/.cache/scourge-pins/investigation-c368ab4d cargo test -p scourge-core --test evidence --locked --offline -- --include-ignored: 7 passed (pinned binary sha256 c368ab4d8e05...)\n- SCOURGE_INVESTIGATION_BIN=<pinned> python3 -B fixtures/contracts/evidence/run.py --adapter fixtures/contracts/evidence/investigation.py: 12/12, OK, no network\n- just m1-recut-check: 55 live KEEP, 0 CUT, 0 SPLIT; 7/7 tests OK (green now; the bn-1rg discrepancy is gone on main)\n- just check: exit 0, 33 test-result-ok groups\n- git diff --check (working tree and ba3b75f..HEAD): PASS\n\nHONEST LIMITS\n- One earlier post-sync `just check` attempt exited 101 in the `teapot_invocation` binary (NativeFailure instead of the expected diagnostic code). That is a pre-existing main-lane flake, not this diff: an extracted tree at base ba3b75f with none of these commits fails the same binary 4 times in 11 runs with the same signature, and this change touches no teapot path. The lead should expect occasional red there.\n- The pinned executable cannot be made to crash on demand, so the crash/signal/timeout/overflow regressions drive controlled children through the same runner and the same `interpret` path; a live backend crash is not claimed.\n- The diagnostic status is reported only when the leader was observed finished before the group kill; a leader that exits in the window between that check and the kill reports status null (conservative).\n- A `Fault::Io`/missing-pipe capture error with no observed status keeps the plain `EvidenceError::Io` kind unchanged rather than gaining a diagnostic. A well-formed error envelope with an unknown code still maps to `Backend`; the envelope itself is the precise signal.\n- The stderr digest and length cover the captured prefix only (64 KiB cap); the excerpt is a redacted prefix of that prefix.\n- No reviewer launch, request, or vote: that stays with the lead."}	blake3:NC_aId6MHi7QKSh1iyhbcISpgXPGZ4z5DypMjM_rXoo
1795541317560771	scourge-show-list	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-r3b	{"body":"WAL startup and snapshot retries are committed at 0799c307606c25fb5b7f2a4b706f1d23d5f4a53e on ba3b75fe41943d2ebfae501c6b5441ac4dbb43ca. Focused, corruption controls and five repeated guarded read-process stress runs passed. Reviewer captured SQLite primary 8 / extended 264 during ordinary concurrent writer commits. The normal full suite reproduced the tracked Teapot launcher fixture flake. Final Seal retarget is held until bn-1rg merges and the ordinary parallel gate passes."}	blake3:sWLrdBlx9GAmH1VsUlR9gsN1SpwSS_XchGoLsiJ8PVc
1795541460154105	scourge-orca-evidence	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1qi	{"body":"Final handoff for the native-review transport blocker: code committed, review retargeted, all evidence validation run. Bone stays doing, claims held, no reviewer requested, no vote cast.\n\nEXACT STATE\n- Workspace .maw/workspaces/bn-1qi HEAD 8f160cc8dcd0a45a586aa00e91c0321eff5e1c87 on base/current main ba3b75fe41943d2ebfae501c6b5441ac4dbb43ca (verified equal to trunk main just now; main did not advance again after the sync).\n- Commits added this turn: 44afbc0 `fix: keep a bounded child's status and stderr diagnostics`, 9c22b5a `chore: record the native review block before the transport fix`, 8f160cc `fix: keep the pre-existing mapping when no child status was observed`. Earlier this turn the clean tree was replayed onto ba3b75f with `maw ws sync bn-1qi` (9 commits, clean, sibling invariant verified); every check below was re-run after that sync and again after 8f160cc.\n- cr-29ocik: anchor detached:8f160cc8dcd0a45a586aa00e91c0321eff5e1c87, base ba3b75fe41943d2ebfae501c6b5441ac4dbb43ca, status open, votes [], 4 open threads all answered and left for the reviewer, reviewers [scourge-security]. No `seal reviews request` was run and no vote was cast.\n- Thread th-187q8s answered twice: th-187q8s.2 (full fix evidence) and th-187q8s.3 (addendum naming the final HEAD 8f160cc and re-validation).\n- Working tree: only .seal/reviews/cr-29ocik/events.jsonl uncommitted (reply + addendum + retarget events written after the final commit; committing them would move HEAD past the retarget target). The merge clean check excludes that path. Nothing was reset, stashed, discarded, pushed, merged, closed, released, re-created or re-requested.\n\nCHANGED ERROR BEHAVIOUR\n- stderr is captured inside the existing 64 KiB cap instead of drained with None; `Output` carries it and it is never echoed.\n- `run` decides with waitid(WNOWAIT|WNOHANG|EXITED) whether the leader had already finished BEFORE it signals the private process group and only then reaps, so a post-leader timeout or overflow keeps the backend's own exit code or signal; this runner's SIGKILL is never reported.\n- New `BackendDiagnostic { status: Option<BackendStatus{Exited,Signaled}>, fault: {Terminated,Timeout,OutputTooLarge}, stderr_bytes, stderr_digest, stderr_excerpt }`; excerpt redacted to printable ASCII, whitespace-collapsed, 200-char cap.\n- `BackendTimeout` and `BackendOutputTooLarge` now carry that diagnostic; new `BackendFailed { diagnostic }` for a nonzero exit or fatal signal without a well-formed error envelope (was `Protocol`).\n- `interpret` keeps `Protocol` only for a malformed reply from a child that exited 0; a well-formed error envelope keeps its typed mapping; a nonzero exit with a receipt-shaped body is no longer accepted as success. Child-handle capture failures with no observed status keep their previous `Backend`/`Io(kind)` mapping (8f160cc).\n- Deadlines (30 s, 5 s version), request/stdout/stderr caps, process-group kill and reap, private 0700 staging with the held 0500 descriptor, ETXTBSY retry, lineage walk and redaction are unchanged.\n\nVALIDATION at 8f160cc / base ba3b75f (TMPDIR=/tmp/scourge-check, CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true)\n- cargo fmt --all -- --check: PASS\n- cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked --offline -- -D warnings: PASS\n- cargo test -p scourge-core --lib --locked --offline: 124 passed, 0 failed; the 18 evidence::transport tests green 3x at this HEAD (plus 5x and 10x at the previous HEADs)\n- SCOURGE_INVESTIGATION_BIN=/home/bob/.cache/scourge-pins/investigation-c368ab4d cargo test -p scourge-core --test evidence --locked --offline -- --include-ignored: 7 passed\n- SCOURGE_INVESTIGATION_BIN=<pinned> python3 -B fixtures/contracts/evidence/run.py --adapter fixtures/contracts/evidence/investigation.py: 12/12, OK, no network\n- just m1-recut-check: 55 live KEEP, 0 CUT, 0 SPLIT; 7/7 tests OK\n- just check: exit 0, 33 test-result-ok groups (unserialized, unweakened)\n- git diff --check (working tree and ba3b75f..HEAD): PASS\n\nGATE FLAKE, RECORDED NOT WORKED AROUND\n- One earlier post-sync `just check` at 9c22b5a/ba3b75f exited 101 in the `teapot_invocation` binary: `wrapper_only_failure_retains_wrapper_exit` expected `ToolUnavailable`, got `NativeFailure`. The gate was not serialized, retried-with-different-args, or relaxed; the same command was simply run again at the same state and passed.\n- Attribution evidence: a clean extracted tree at base ba3b75f with none of these commits reproduces the same `NativeFailure` signature in 4 of 11 runs, across different tests in that binary, and this diff touches no teapot path. Consistent with the independently proven fixture race the lead described; the final gate run above was green.\n\nHONEST LIMITS\n- The pinned executable cannot be made to crash on demand, so the crash/signal/timeout/overflow regressions drive controlled children through the same runner and the same `interpret` path; no live backend crash is claimed.\n- Status is reported only when the leader was observed finished before the group kill; a leader exiting in the window between that check and the kill reports status null.\n- The stderr digest and length cover the captured prefix only (64 KiB cap); the excerpt is a redacted prefix of that prefix.\n- A well-formed error envelope with an unknown code still maps to `Backend`; the envelope is the precise signal.\n- The three original review threads plus th-187q8s stay open for the reviewer to resolve; independent lead review, sync of the launcher fix and final approval remain with the lead."}	blake3:EwdP6RWoKRJ_Mb3i30SPaESRNXBczgNOcR1XLsLGaa4
