1795543634579379	scourge-orca-evidence	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1qi	{"body":"REVIEW HANDOFF — sync onto current main, evidence re-verified, threads left for the reviewer\n\nEXACT STATE\n- Workspace bn-1qi, final HEAD 561bb6d23099a5a4d051622c42b5a191384362ad, base (fork point) fdcb1996683524de2f700cd2e71069ba5b2b8bd2, which is current local main.\n- Sync: `maw ws sync bn-1qi` replayed 11 branch commits from base ba3b75fe41943d2ebfae501c6b5441ac4dbb43ca onto fdcb199 and reported \"Rebase complete: 11 commit(s) replayed cleanly\" with zero conflicts, so no conflict resolution was needed and none was invented. The replay recorded the invariant check \"verified 3 sibling workspace(s) — no committed work orphaned\".\n- One commit was required to sync at all: the retained `.seal/reviews/cr-29ocik/events.jsonl` was uncommitted and Maw refuses to replay over a dirty tree. It was committed unmodified as 7fd3e569872b (\"chore: record cr-29ocik retarget to 8f160cc before syncing onto main\"), matching the branch's existing precedent. No other commit was made.\n- No reset, no stash, no discard, no recreation, no branch, no push.\n- cr-29ocik: status open, target 561bb6d, base fdcb199, votes [], reviewers [scourge-security]. Retargeted once to the final target; retarget is the only review-state change I made. I did not resolve any thread, did not re-request reviewers, and did not vote or block.\n\nWHAT THE SYNC DID NOT CHANGE\nEvery evidence source and test file is byte-identical at 561bb6d to the previously reviewed 8f160cc8dcd0a45a586aa00e91c0321eff5e1c87: `crates/scourge-core/src/evidence/capture.rs`, `lineage.rs`, `mod.rs`, `transport.rs`, `transport/process.rs`, and `crates/scourge-core/tests/evidence.rs`. Only `Cargo.lock` overlapped main's own ba3b75f..fdcb199 delta; the merged lockfile is valid, adds only `base64 0.22.1` to `scourge-core`, keeps a single `rustix 1.1.6` entry, and has no duplicate package names. Main's other changes landed beside this diff untouched.\n\nALL FOUR THREADS RE-CHECKED AGAINST THE SYNCED CODE\nth-3memt0 (complete lineage), th-1s7lr2 (transport bounds), th-20x0u4 (private staging), th-187q8s (failure evidence) each have a reply on the thread recording the current code locations and the tests that exercise them at 561bb6d. The guarantees named in those replies are unchanged by the replay: complete-lineage refusal bounded at 256 records, per-call deadlines and stream caps, private 0700 staging with the held 0500 descriptor, the bounded ETXTBSY retry, redacted bounded diagnostics with status preservation, and typed errors throughout.\n\nVALIDATION AT THIS EXACT TARGET (fresh runs after the sync)\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: PASS.\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`: PASS.\n- `cargo test -p scourge-core --lib --locked`: 129 passed, 0 failed (18 `evidence::transport*` regressions green).\n- `SCOURGE_INVESTIGATION_BIN=/home/bob/.cache/scourge-pins/investigation-c368ab4d cargo test -p scourge-core --test evidence --locked -- --include-ignored`: 7 passed, 0 failed, including `withdrawal_beyond_native_lineage_scan_refuses_every_use` (65 derivatives).\n- Frozen qualification replay: 12/12, OK, no network.\n- `just m1-recut-check`: 55 live KEEP, 0 CUT, 0 SPLIT, 7/7 tests OK.\n- `just check`: exit 0 on the first attempt, 33 `test result: ok` groups, run normally in parallel with no serialization. `teapot_invocation` was 13 passed / 0 failed / 3 ignored in this run, so the fixture flake recorded earlier did not recur.\n- `git diff --check` on the working tree and on `main..HEAD`: PASS.\n\nFROZEN INVESTIGATION IDENTITY RE-VERIFIED\n`git archive --format=tar 6a0c5ed843d0f4870910d3a926298890290c916e` in the Investigation repo reproduces the recorded archive digest 12efb99c978e10f634f43b039ddc5391de5dbfeb44bcd4703952fb1aae0415df. The tree the pinned binary was built from diffs clean against that archive, all 1447 files. Binary sha256 at /home/bob/.cache/scourge-pins/investigation-c368ab4d is c368ab4d8e0511524674692b039c4f248cee2b5676d143a23f5ab9025a31d4fc, matching the committed conformance record.\n\nHONEST LIMITS\n- The lineage walk is bounded at 256 current records and refuses conservatively beyond that; it is exercised live to 65, not to the bound. `source.withdraw` is exercised deeply only structurally and directly only in the shallow regression. Concurrent writers, power loss, retention and export remain outside the qualified scope, as docs/adr/evidence-contract.md records.\n- One 30 s deadline covers each call; a very large lineage walk could refuse with `BackendTimeout` instead of completing. That is a refusal, not a silent pass.\n- Executing through `/proc/self/fd/<n>` requires procfs; a host without it fails rather than falling back to path-based exec.\n- Redaction keeps only printable ASCII, so a non-ASCII backend diagnostic is identifiable only by its length and digest.\n- `just check` runs the live evidence tests as ignored because `SCOURGE_INVESTIGATION_BIN` is not set in the gate; they were run separately above against the pinned binary. The gate itself was not serialized, relaxed or bypassed.\n- The working tree is intentionally left dirty with the retarget and these replies in `.seal/reviews/cr-29ocik/events.jsonl`; the merge clean check excludes that path. No bone or workspace claim was released and nothing was destroyed."}	blake3:30KKEDBEViJSh32RKGgXAX8JA1iWyl5MfiN4AB4K9a0
