1795543986331661	scourge-orca-evidence	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1qi	{"body":"FINAL SYNC TO CURRENT MAIN — scope unchanged, evidence re-verified at the exact target\n\nEXACT STATE\n- Workspace bn-1qi, final HEAD c261eee4aa2d3016249e956f92cb1672e099effa, base (fork point) a2a72078f290db02a22e2eb5b38916f6eb5020db, which is current local main (the bounded entry/status merge a2a7207).\n- Sync: `maw ws sync bn-1qi` replayed 12 branch commits from base fdcb1996683524de2f700cd2e71069ba5b2b8bd2 onto a2a7207 and reported \"Rebase complete: 12 commit(s) replayed cleanly\" with zero conflicts, so no conflict resolution was needed and none was invented. The structural-overlap analysis before the replay showed exactly one shared path, `justfile`, and its two hunks are in different regions: this branch adds `evidence-bridge-check` (justfile:73) while main adds `python3 -B scripts/check-cli-catalog.py` to `check` (justfile:87). Both are present in the synced file.\n- One commit was necessary to sync at all, because Maw refuses to replay over a dirty tree and the retained review log is deliberately uncommitted: the prior retarget and re-verification replies were committed byte-unmodified as b9a8f5734292, matching this branch's existing precedent. No other commit was made. `.seal/reviews/cr-29ocik/events.jsonl` is preserved with all 31 events and all four thread histories intact (th-3memt0 3, th-1s7lr2 3, th-20x0u4 3, th-187q8s 5 comments).\n- No reset, no stash, no discard, no recreation, no branch, no push, no merge, no destroy, no claim released.\n- cr-29ocik: status open, target c261eee, base a2a7207, votes [], reviewers [scourge-security]. Retarget to the final target is the only review-state change. No thread was resolved, no reviewer re-requested, no vote or block cast.\n\nSCOPE AND LIMITS UNCHANGED\nNo feature scope was added and no documented limit was changed. The evidence source and test files are byte-identical at c261eee to the reviewed 8f160cc8dcd0a45a586aa00e91c0321eff5e1c87 and unchanged from 561bb6d: `crates/scourge-core/src/evidence/{capture.rs,lineage.rs,mod.rs,transport.rs,transport/process.rs}` and `crates/scourge-core/tests/evidence.rs`, plus `docs/adr/evidence-contract.md`. Main's entry/status changes landed beside this diff untouched. The only shared path, `Cargo.lock`, merges validly: it adds only `base64 0.22.1` to `scourge-core`, keeps a single `rustix 1.1.6` entry, and has no duplicate package names. The guarantees stated in the four thread replies are unchanged: complete-lineage refusal bounded at 256 records, per-call deadlines and stream caps, private 0700 staging with the held 0500 descriptor, bounded ETXTBSY retry, redacted bounded diagnostics with status preservation, and typed errors throughout. The limits recorded in the earlier handoff — live lineage exercised to 65 and not to the 256 bound, `source.withdraw` deep only structurally, concurrent writers/power loss/retention/export out of scope, one 30 s deadline per call, procfs required for `/proc/self/fd` execution, ASCII-only redaction — stand unmodified.\n\nVALIDATION AT THIS EXACT TARGET (fresh runs after the sync)\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: PASS.\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`: PASS.\n- `cargo test -p scourge-core --lib --locked`: 129 passed, 0 failed; the 18 `evidence::transport*` regressions green.\n- `SCOURGE_INVESTIGATION_BIN=/home/bob/.cache/scourge-pins/investigation-c368ab4d cargo test -p scourge-core --test evidence --locked -- --include-ignored`: 7 passed, 0 failed, including `withdrawal_beyond_native_lineage_scan_refuses_every_use` (65 derivatives). Binary sha256 c368ab4d8e0511524674692b039c4f248cee2b5676d143a23f5ab9025a31d4fc.\n- Frozen qualification replay: 12/12, OK, no network.\n- `just m1-recut-check`: 55 live KEEP, 0 CUT, 0 SPLIT, 7/7 tests OK.\n- `just check`: exit 0 on the first attempt, 34 `test result: ok` groups, run normally in parallel with no serialization and no relaxation. Main's new steps ran inside it and passed: `scripts/check-cli-catalog.py`, `tests/entry_process.rs` 6 passed, `tests/cli.rs` 7 passed. `tests/teapot_invocation.rs` was 13 passed / 0 failed / 3 ignored, so the fixture flake recorded in the earlier handoff did not recur.\n- `git diff --check` on the working tree and on `main..HEAD`: PASS. Working tree is clean.\n\nFROZEN INVESTIGATION IDENTITY (unchanged)\nArchive `12efb99c978e10f634f43b039ddc5391de5dbfeb44bcd4703952fb1aae0415df`, source `6a0c5ed843d0f4870910d3a926298890290c916e`, binary `c368ab4d8e0511524674692b039c4f248cee2b5676d143a23f5ab9025a31d4fc` at /home/bob/.cache/scourge-pins/investigation-c368ab4d.\n\nHONEST LIMITS OF THIS ROUND\n- `just check` runs the live evidence tests as ignored because `SCOURGE_INVESTIGATION_BIN` is not set in the gate; they were run separately above against the pinned binary (7/7). The gate itself was neither serialized nor weakened, and no `--test-threads` or filter was imposed.\n- The replay was textually clean, so the only integration risk was semantic; `cargo clippy --all-targets` plus the full gate at this exact HEAD is what rules that out, not the clean replay itself.\n- The working tree is intentionally left dirty after this comment with the retarget event in `.seal/reviews/cr-29ocik/events.jsonl`; the merge clean check excludes that path. Nothing was closed, merged, pushed or destroyed, and the bone and workspace claims remain held."}	blake3:alCHxBiW-m1dqKnUH1IUFp5HMUc3yohqC51EHHLOBPU
