1795545039698646	scourge-orca-teapot	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3s5	{"body":"Cyber-capable remediation progress, bone remains doing. Exact HEAD 39913ba41e67b928afa7c6c7e5e5967088e9fc0c on base 54a567b79d7369cc2e2de4dd591b3eab239df04c (current main). Preserved the previous exact target 47cdb5b5fd1255df49f6789cb0daa46b4b4c3db6 and the cr-vprkb6 event log (sha256 e0e2266a67e08a674dbd100ab6b9701fcde59b1f809944af0e91bb6926bd8431 unchanged through the sync), then Maw sync replayed the workspace onto epoch 54a567b; the replay conflicted only on the base64 pin in Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, crates/scourge-core/Cargo.toml and scripts/check-dependency-pins.py, resolved with maw ws resolve --keep epoch so those files are byte-identical to main, plus one docs-only follow-up (39913ba) putting the stored-body base64 row back on 0.22.1. Fixed only cr-vprkb6's three P1 threads: th-3dpbxz real frozen relogin/retry shapes (reply flow and StepRun.flow are the retry, logged_out_flow is the original send, retried with retry_flow=null is FlowReference::Missing); th-336x97 literal @-prefixed body and --set values escaped as @@ per the frozen resolve/localize contract so Teapot cannot open a host file, plus NUL rejected as InvalidArgument before spawn; th-3rh4jz requested --follow and --until effect bounds and successful-reply topology (1..=1+follow complete hops; unbounded run all steps complete; --until N sends 1..=N and only later steps are not-run with null flow/status; replay sends all preparatory and replayed steps) so extra traffic and false NotSent are typed InvalidNativeOutput. Validation on 39913ba: cargo fmt --all --check clean; clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -D warnings clean; 23 focused teapot_invocation tests; 5/5 digest-pinned Teapot tests with SCOURGE_PINNED_TEAPOT=/tmp/scourge-bn-1b4-target/debug/teapot sha256 6d15d625e10afa768a221f64eb7a2a245a64a7babbe61cf74ce8d4ff33b2f458 (including a new live follow-chain, --until 1 and literal @-body/edit/replay case); just m1-recut-check; full normal parallel just check. Review cr-vprkb6 retargeted to 39913ba on base 54a567b with fresh votes required, three P1 threads replied with exact evidence and left open for reviewer resolution, working tree clean except the excluded .seal/reviews/cr-vprkb6/events.jsonl. Limits: M0.7 macro_replay capture is still null and only the two-step shape is live-qualified; capture-lost mid-flow is not injected (retry/login-shared variants are fixture-driven); flow heads are rendered text; destination is derived from the recorded URL; no durable caller per-send reference beyond the nullable flow ID; a non-retried logged_out_flow from a followed redirect is recorded as reported. Not requested, voted, closed, merged, pushed, released or destroyed."}	blake3:MbrpON_Oy_f3EEoCQy85HVe2iexYI8tTdYCy-n4dPOI
1795545704927394	scourge-suggested-argv	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-23h	{"body":"Review fixes committed at 7c898973998fa560fcae2eae7c7bf98ca3d5211b on base 54a567b79d7369cc2e2de4dd591b3eab239df04c. Replaced hard-coded seeds with recursive Clap command/alias/argument/error-path discovery; exact Option scope preservation now rejects dropped workspace or engagement; added version-emission and scope-loss negative witnesses; production help action is explicitly unscoped. Disposable version-action mutation was discovered/launched. cargo test -p scourge --test entry_process --locked, cargo test -p scourge --test cli --locked, just m1-recut-check, normal parallel just check, cargo fmt/clippy, and git diff --check pass. Replied to th-3bqv6q/th-eq5sy6 and retargeted/re-requested cr-27kkrl at exact HEAD/base. Bone remains doing with claims held for fresh native review."}	blake3:EsD-pavYUaSx5e9p-Wn3xHMNOqL95P2dTklHEIj_yF4
1795545836732681	scourge-orca-fuzz	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2ai	{"body":"HANDOFF (cyber implementation owner, scourge-orca-fuzz). Bone left doing, needs-cyber, claims held; no self-vote, no finish, no merge, no push.\n\nExact state\n- workspace: /home/bob/src/scourge/.maw/workspaces/bn-2ai\n- HEAD: eb8a0d7101f95da60b558cded23c0eaf30570e5d, working tree clean\n- local main/base: 54a567b79d7369cc2e2de4dd591b3eab239df04c (after the Investigation evidence merge)\n- Seal review: cr-3oiz60, base 54a567b, target ba7400aa1e27c669f551d33c325fea71e3acc75a, reviewers [scourge-security], 0 votes, 0 open threads. The single commit after the target (eb8a0d7) touches only .seal/reviews/cr-3oiz60/events.jsonl.\n- history: 8e64479 handoff -> 1b0402a (preserved handoff verbatim) -> 1ef9575 (harness, targets, corpus, guards) -> 84b5e86 (maw conflict resolution; removes five bookkeeping comment lines only) -> 9e452fe (session record) -> ba7400a (corpus .gitattributes) -> eb8a0d7 (review log).\n\nAcceptance\n- six pinned cargo-fuzz targets: canonical_json, wire_contracts, declarations, teapot_output, oracle_observations, body_decoder. libfuzzer-sys =0.4.13 is optional behind the `fuzzing` feature, required by every target, so the stable toolchain never links libFuzzer.\n- invariants: duplicate keys always rejected (INV-44, including \\uXXXX spelling); accepted bytes canonical round-trip; stored requests equal their wire envelope; every declaration rejection names a schema-owned stanza and never echoes input; malformed/non-zero/signal Teapot output is a typed contract error and never a pass, with strict acceptance a subset of adapter acceptance; oracle verdicts are never derived from incomplete evidence and an oracle panic fails the harness; body decoding stays inside the size and ratio bounds with typed DecodeError. Every path is typed and has no effect.\n- corpus: 99 seeds from fixtures/contracts and the development fixture, with one boundary/negative per parser; replay asserts each seed's exact typed outcome and that every target has both an accepted and a rejected seed.\n- non-vacuity: fuzz/tests/witnesses.rs proves each of the 13 Teapot shapes parses its own contract and rejects the others (one documented rules/intercept-rules overlap), proves the three declaration shapes are not interchangeable, and pins every body/oracle boundary.\n- docs: fuzz/README.md (operator guide) and docs/fuzzing.md (recorded sessions and their limits).\n- pins: scripts/check-dependency-pins.py now also checks the cargo-fuzz metadata, the fuzzing feature gate, target declarations, per-target seed corpora and the single nightly toolchain in the justfile; docs/dependencies.md records it.\n\nRecorded bounded run (2026-11-24, revision 1ef9575, clean tree, nightly-2026-08-21 + cargo-fuzz 0.13.1, offline, -max_len=16384 -timeout=5 -rss_limit_mb=1024): 90 s bound per target, 91 s reported, zero crashes, timeouts or OOM. Runs: canonical 509926, wire 255368, declarations 347405, teapot 43115, oracle 2077193, body 837098. Nothing to minimize; no generated unit was checked in. This is a sample, not a proof of exhaustiveness.\n\nGates at HEAD eb8a0d7: cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings, just parser-corpus-check (replay + witnesses), just m1-recut-check, just deps-check, and full just check all pass. The fuzz harness was built and run under the pinned nightly before trusting it (E0716 and a fuzz-created malformed duplicate were found and fixed).\n\nLeft for the fresh native reviewer: review the persisted range 54a567b..ba7400a with seal review/diff (six invalid-UTF-8 corpus entries and raw coded bodies are marked binary in .gitattributes, read them with xxd or the replay test), check the harness against the frozen contracts, and vote. The remaining bone acceptance boxes are satisfied by the above; the reviewer should confirm rather than repeat the sessions."}	blake3:4yu7zrvNqUyeD6aibIF-iBlzF1EP9AQf9kOrOZJ3Vlo
1795546047506430	scourge-orca-fuzz	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2ai	{"body":"Correction to the handoff above: the authoritative review is cr-3cu3tb (open, base 54a567b79d7369cc2e2de4dd591b3eab239df04c, target eb8a0d7101f95da60b558cded23c0eaf30570e5d, reviewers [scourge-security], 0 votes, 0 open threads). cr-3oiz60 is abandoned: it was created with base a2a7207, which would have included the sibling Investigation evidence merge, and it is superseded before any vote. HEAD is eb8a0d7 and the only working-tree changes are uncommitted Seal metadata (.seal/reviews/cr-3oiz60/events.jsonl modified, .seal/reviews/cr-3cu3tb/ untracked); no code file differs from eb8a0d7. just check re-run green in this exact state."}	blake3:Tw2sJMZnh3ctLhQppFAspQT82kbXM5jvOfHyNGtLey0
