1795546277383202	scourge-orca-teapot	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3s5	{"body":"Second native BLOCK remediated, bone remains doing, workspace and claims held for review. Exact HEAD 1610e947aa4d40bb60126f827eb2c3f64e192821 on base 54a567b79d7369cc2e2de4dd591b3eab239df04c (current main). The preserved target 39913ba41e67b928afa7c6c7e5e5967088e9fc0c, the modified .seal/reviews/cr-vprkb6/events.jsonl and all thread history were kept as they were; no reset, stash, revert, recreate, merge, push or release. One commit (1610e94) changes exactly two files: crates/scourge-core/src/teapot/send.rs and crates/scourge-core/tests/teapot_invocation.rs.\n\nFixed exactly the three P1 threads:\n- th-3dpbxz: the repository-recorded paused-after-retry relogin shape (action=paused, ran=true, paused=true, retried=true, logged_out_flow=10, login_flows=[11], retry_flow=12 in fixtures/contracts/channel-observed.txt) is accepted. The guessed ran<->action table is replaced by the one frozen impossibility (login-shared+ran=true), with frozen citations for the other ran=false/ran=true shapes (decided_locked waiter copy, Ended::CannotRun), and retried=true is now restricted to re-logged-in/login-shared/paused. Original=logged_out_flow, Login=login_flows, Retry=final flow and the INV-41 Missing-retry case are preserved. The recorded envelope is parsed from the repo fixture, not typed in, for send and for StepRun.\n- th-336x97: no-equals and equals path:/method: edits are escaped, because edit/parse.rs resolves rest.strip_prefix('=').unwrap_or(rest) for both; source-free json-/form-/query-/cookie- are byte-identical, path:/a=b stays one path, equal-form json/json+/form/query/cookie/header behaviour and the exact @@ literal encoding and NUL refusal are unchanged.\n- th-3rh4jz: post---until NotRun suffix rows may carry no answer-derived field (status, class, reason, relogin/login flows, set, withheld, csrf_refreshed), matching frozen StepReport::new, so MacroRun::flows cannot report traffic for a NotSent step; declaration metadata (method, url, state_changing, compute, references) still parses, and the earlier follow/until counts, complete prefixes and error-envelope rules are unchanged.\n\nPrior three fixes preserved: exact stored-flow reads with body windows, owned-job cancellation with independent observation, and send/macro/replay with the nullable flow ID, DispatchEvidence::NoFlow distinct from NotSent and login/retry flows bound to their step.\n\nValidation on 1610e94: cargo fmt --all -- --check clean; clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -D warnings clean; 23 focused teapot_invocation tests; 5/5 digest-pinned Teapot tests with SCOURGE_PINNED_TEAPOT=/tmp/scourge-bn-1b4-target/debug/teapot (sha256 6d15d625e10afa768a221f64eb7a2a245a64a7babbe61cf74ce8d4ff33b2f458 = fixtures/contracts/manifest.json), including a live follow chain, --until 1, literal @ body/edit/replay and the new path:@/method:@ sentinel refusals; just m1-recut-check; full normal parallel just check (exit 0); git diff --check clean; working tree clean except the excluded .seal/reviews/cr-vprkb6/events.jsonl.\n\nNon-vacuity: two deliberate mutation checks. Reverting only the new path/method escaping makes the pinned test fail after Teapot reads the sentinel, and compiling out the NotRun check makes the focused test accept class=2xx on a NotSent step.\n\nReview: cr-vprkb6 retargeted from 39913ba to 1610e94 on base 54a567b with the reviewer's block vote cleared, fresh votes required; th-3dpbxz.5, th-336x97.5, th-3rh4jz.6 replied with exact evidence and left open for reviewer resolution, plus a target/scope/limits update on th-1ffu9j.6. Limiting evidence unchanged: macro_replay M0.7 registry capture is still null and only the tested two-step shape is live-qualified; capture-lost mid-flow is not injected; relogin variants are record/fixture-driven because the pinned fixture does not rotate a session to logged-out; flow heads are rendered text; destination is derived from the recorded URL; no durable caller per-send reference beyond the nullable flow ID. Not requested again, voted, closed, merged, pushed, released or destroyed."}	blake3:73Ly6_VLdmEuzuLXsZzQkG83q3rEZDjgYHVQZq9n7BA
