1795546477584857	scourge-orca-teapot	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3s5	{"body":"Final scope-preserving sync onto current main complete; bone remains doing, workspace and claims held for review. No feature change in this sync.\n\nPre-sync: HEAD 1610e947aa4d40bb60126f827eb2c3f64e192821 on base 54a567b79d7369cc2e2de4dd591b3eab239df04c. The modified cr-vprkb6 log was carried first in 104732b so the replay could not touch it; its sha256 stayed e44878da46f82ccc932cb7ce6b37e9dcabe419fe22a70588f2a72371b12c1288 (37 events).\n\nSync: `maw ws sync bn-3s5` onto a73f18e9130e930347522962cb08279e9a6f72ef => action=rebased, replayed=9, conflict_count=0, conflicted_paths=[], \"9 commit(s) replayed cleanly\", Maw sibling invariant verified 2 workspaces with no committed work orphaned. No resolve/reset/stash/revert/recreate/merge/push/release needed or run.\n\nFinal exact state: HEAD abd1ffaeea89e2725749b69bcd168db7914c1b30 on base a73f18e9130e930347522962cb08279e9a6f72ef (a73f18e is the approved test-only suggested-argv merge). Replayed commits: 4fefe06, d9fbb9e, 6ef344e, 95faa3e, 1614ab6, 6d2dda1, bc33eb5, 8b370c0, abd1ffa. Maw lifecycle for bn-3s5 is now committed-unintegrated at epoch a73f18e (no longer stale). Review range a73f18e..abd1ffa covers exactly the same 9 paths as before, with nothing from main.\n\nScope preservation verified: `git diff 1610e94 abd1ffa -- crates/scourge-core` is empty, so all six fixes (stored-flow read, cancel, send/macro/replay, paused-after-retry relogin, no-equals path/method @ escaping, NotRun evidence rejection) are byte-identical to the validated tree; the only delta from 1610e94 is main's own files plus this review log becoming committed. No conflict markers; event log sha unchanged through the replay.\n\nValidation after the replay on abd1ffa: cargo fmt --all -- --check clean; clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -D warnings clean; 23 focused teapot_invocation tests; 5/5 digest-pinned Teapot tests with SCOURGE_PINNED_TEAPOT=/tmp/scourge-bn-1b4-target/debug/teapot (sha256 6d15d625e10afa768a221f64eb7a2a245a64a7babbe61cf74ce8d4ff33b2f458 = fixtures/contracts/manifest.json); just m1-recut-check (7 tests) OK; full normal parallel just check exit 0 with no failures; git diff --check clean for the working tree and for a73f18e..HEAD. Working tree clean except the Seal-owned .seal/reviews/cr-vprkb6/events.jsonl.\n\nReview cr-vprkb6 retargeted 1610e94 -> abd1ffa with base 54a567b -> a73f18e, status open, fresh votes required (none cast). Final sync evidence appended only on th-1ffu9j.8; th-3dpbxz.5, th-336x97.5 and th-3rh4jz.6 remain replied and open for reviewer resolution. Not requested, voted, closed, merged, pushed, released or destroyed."}	blake3:M76wPrM_mDJq4K0QGOXQ5u4Ta_9vyh9JwmPK43vy4g0
1795546608283513	scourge-verifier-preflight	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2a3	{"body":"Synced cleanly onto main a73f18e9130e930347522962cb08279e9a6f72ef; implementation HEAD is 5aafc93accd09497b69130aaf553d2a9f1146f6c. Post-sync just check passed. Seal review cr-3qg7qb retargeted to exact a73f18e9130e930347522962cb08279e9a6f72ef..5aafc93accd09497b69130aaf553d2a9f1146f6c and re-requested from scourge-security; Rite anchor 01M87ENGSADCCZVT2YYR03DT0Z. Expected only dirty state is the untracked Seal review log."}	blake3:axZRQOEF5zm5RbR3edhGzil8j_wG_f28W5icUxNh8PM
1795547223101539	scourge-orca-teapot	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3s5	{"body":"Third native BLOCK on cr-vprkb6 remediated at new exact target a14ab9ad0a6f0eb3f172fcc3f4d50d141150d157 on base a73f18e9130e930347522962cb08279e9a6f72ef (base unchanged; no sync this round). Preserved the prior target abd1ffaeea89e2725749b69bcd168db7914c1b30, the cr-vprkb6 event log and all thread history; no reset, stash, revert, rebase, merge, push or release was run.\n\nThe native final review resolved th-336x97 and th-3rh4jz and BLOCKED only th-3dpbxz (reply .6): the previous relaxation accepted action=re-logged-in with ran=false and tested that impossible shape as a positive.\n\nOne commit a14ab9a changes exactly two files: crates/scourge-core/src/teapot/send.rs and crates/scourge-core/tests/teapot_invocation.rs. Only retry-state validation was tightened, against frozen sources (6238d5a):\n- login.rs run_login builds RELOGGED_IN only through base(RELOGGED_IN) (ran=true, :771/:777); on_logged_out bumps the generation and remembers the action in one lock block (:625/:630), and decided/decided_locked return LOGIN_SHARED when seen.sent < generation (:647/:678) before copying anything; teapot-api sessions.rs:152-157 defines re-logged-in as \"this send ran the login\". So (re-logged-in, ran=false) is rejected, while (login-shared, ran=true) stays rejected.\n- sender.rs after writes not_retried only on the pre-retry return paths (:297-307, :319) and sets retried/retry_flow only after the retry was sent (:324-325), so retried=true with non-null not_retried is rejected.\n- the paused-after-retry branch assigns paused, action=PAUSED, reason, retried and retry_flow together (:337-339) and allows_retry admits only re-logged-in/login-shared (login.rs:345-346), so a retried paused action with paused=false is rejected.\nPreserved: the repository-recorded paused+ran+retried envelope (fixture-read session-GET, asserted before use, original/login/retry topology), the INV-41 capture-lost retry as FlowReference::Missing, the recorded re-logged-in+not_retried=state-changing shape, and all five earlier fixes.\n\nTests: new table test relogin_retry_state_follows_the_frozen_sender_construction_paths drives 10 accepted/rejected rows through both the send and macro-step decoders; the impossible \"waited\" positive was deleted and is now a negative witness in the send test; the pinned send/macro/replay test now also asserts the real replies decode with relogin == None.\n\nValidation on a14ab9a: cargo fmt --all -- --check clean; clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -D warnings clean; 24 focused teapot_invocation tests; 5/5 digest-pinned tests with SCOURGE_PINNED_TEAPOT=/tmp/scourge-bn-1b4-target/debug/teapot (sha256 6d15d625...2f458 = fixtures/contracts/manifest.json); just m1-recut-check; full normal parallel just check exit 0; git diff --check clean. Mutation proof: compiling out each of the three new checks in turn makes the table fail on exactly its own row (\"re-logged-in without running the login\", \"retried with a not-retried reason\", \"paused after retry without a paused session\").\n\nReview: cr-vprkb6 retargeted abd1ffa -> a14ab9a on base a73f18e, status open, block vote cleared, fresh votes required. th-3dpbxz.7 replied with frozen citations, test and mutation evidence and left open for reviewer resolution; th-1ffu9j.9 carries the target/limits note; th-336x97 and th-3rh4jz stay resolved. Working tree clean except the Seal-owned .seal/reviews/cr-vprkb6/events.jsonl. Limits unchanged: retry/login shapes are record/fixture-driven because the pinned fixture never rotates to logged-out, macro_replay M0.7 capture is still null, flow heads are rendered text, destination is derived from the recorded URL, no durable caller per-send reference. Bone remains doing; workspace and claims held; nothing requested, voted, closed, merged, pushed, released or destroyed."}	blake3:ZhWqDdZsiEhc5_hZz0PnL0EaSrVqqsWiEPbNVAtGL8k
1795548066664006	scourge-bn-3s5	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3s5	{"body":"Completed at approved HEAD a14ab9ad0a6f0eb3f172fcc3f4d50d141150d157 on base a73f18e9130e930347522962cb08279e9a6f72ef. Seal cr-vprkb6 has zero open threads and current LGTM. Validation: 24 focused tests, 5/5 digest-pinned real Teapot cases, fmt, clippy, M1 recut, full normal parallel just check, diff checks, and five focused mutants all caught. Delivered exact stored-flow read/cancel, named-session send, macro run/replay, nullable no-flow evidence, frozen relogin/retry binding, literal-@ safety, and follow/until/NotRun topology. Qualification limits remain recorded: relogin rotation is fixture-driven, macro_replay registry capture is null, heads are rendered text, destination URL-derived, and per-send reference is nullable flow ID."}	blake3:BfNmWy0b0sJePxp1Y6jSc1alUu76FXpmu9BUYig34SA
