1795549125569931	scourge-orca-fuzz	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2ai	{"body":"RESUME + FIX HANDOFF (scourge-orca-fuzz). Bone left doing, no merge/push/request/vote/resolve/close/destroy.\n\nExact state\n- workspace: /home/bob/src/scourge/.maw/workspaces/bn-2ai\n- HEAD: 5d7b225686f7d49c7080e4360b4f22bf0fa61e8e, tree clean except the review events written after the last commit\n- range base: c6f7be036846646230f4ceeb9f21d7bc7dba72d0 (trunk advanced a73f18e -> c6f7be0 \"complete Teapot action adapter\" while this review was open; maw replayed the workspace onto it)\n- review cr-3cu3tb: open, base c6f7be0, target 5d7b225, reviewers [scourge-security], 0 votes (retarget cleared the old block and requires a fresh vote), 3 open P1 threads each with a fix reply, th-2r7stv carries the range/coverage correction. No new request was sent.\n- uncommitted: .seal/reviews/cr-3cu3tb/events.jsonl (ReviewRetargeted + the four replies). Everything else is committed. Prior reviewed target eb8a0d7 is preserved under refs/reviews/bn-2ai/target-eb8a0d7 because the replay rewrote commit hashes; the abandoned cr-3oiz60 log is committed.\n- corpus: 105 seeds. All 99 original seeds are byte-identical; additions are one minimized crash regression (declarations/array-root-unsafe-number.json) and five fixture-derived action captures.\n\nCommit range c6f7be0..5d7b225 (12): 05e5c1c preserved handoff, 34257e3 harness+targets, 8ab36d1 maw resolution, 992a5dc session record, 37d5a52 corpus gitattributes, 8ac4e91 + f26ce9e review logs, b141890 the three P1 fixes, 92b2731 index-only stanza + crash seed, 2990e83 cancel.rs decode adaptation (necessary trunk conflict), c8c93e2 live action reply coverage, 5d7b225 smoke record.\n\nP1 fixes (each with the reviewer's mutation as a checked-in test)\n- th-1dv0mz: entries return a typed Outcome trace; ENTRIES/stages() is the contract; corpus_replay asserts the exact stage trace and typed decision per seed through the same function the libFuzzer binary calls; targets.rs statically requires each fuzz_targets/*.rs to call its own entry once; witnesses run the same replay with an immediate-return entry and a foreign entry and require failure. `return Outcome::default()` in all six entries now fails 12 replay tests (was 30 green).\n- th-2b9qrt: scourge_core::is_schema_stanza validates the actual frozen field grammar/roots; the harness uses it for every rejection. The claim-template witness injects template_extension, requires the wildcard `*`, requires the key absent from the diagnostic, and asserts the entry records the same. Leaking that key fails the witness; leaking any unknown key fails the corpus replay.\n- th-3n39q4: scripts/check-fuzz-toolchain.py holds the only pin (cargo-fuzz 0.13.1) and `just fuzz-parsers` runs it before the scratch corpus, compile or launch; scripts/test-fuzz-toolchain.py drives a PATH shim reporting 99.0.0 (checker refuses with only `fuzz --version` in the shim log) and the real recipe end to end; deps-check pins the checker, docs and check-before-launch order. The smokes below ran through the enforcing recipe.\n\nLive action reply surfaces (lead-directed, not silently omitted)\n- NativeOutput now names all 18 argv outputs; teapot_output has 23 stages: 18 shape decodes plus 5 typed replies (requests send, macros run, flows replay, flows show, jobs stop).\n- The trailing typed-reply parsers are the adapter's own decoders, exposed through scourge-core's new `hostile-input` feature (enabled only by the fuzz crate; no process, network or state). Trusted operator parameters come from fuzz/src/lib.rs::action_cases at the values each captured seed was recorded with.\n- Seeds: send.json (fixtures/contracts/send.json, live send, alice, flow 3), macro-run.json (macro-send.json), macro-replay.json (the two captured macro steps arranged as the checked-in replay_output fixture, flow 5/step 2), flows-show.json (read-flow.json, flow 3, 0..32 KiB), jobs-stop.json (checked-in stop reply, job 41 ending/stopped_now), jobs-stop-empty.json (cancel.json --all, schema-valid but no acknowledgment). Provenance is in fuzz/README.md.\n- Witnesses: 18x18 wrong-shape matrix with the two schema overlaps (send/send_dry_run, macro_run/macro_dry_run) plus rules/intercept; each live reply parses to its typed shape with its fields; 27 contradiction cases refused (dry run, hop list past the follow bound, flow/status disagreement, wrong session, step/unit arithmetic, replay parent, body-window/base64 mismatch, missing origin, wrong job, non-frozen wait, engine not running, no job row, two job rows, terminal state without a stop); signal and non-zero exits refused; another action's reply never satisfies a different action.\n\nGates at 5d7b225 (all green)\n- cargo fmt --all -- --check; cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings\n- just parser-corpus-check: 19 replay tests + 2 target invariants + 20 witnesses\n- just fuzz-tooling-check: 6 tests incl. the end-to-end `just fuzz-parsers canonicaljson 1` refusal\n- just deps-check (25 pins, 6 targets, cargo-fuzz 0.13.1, hostile-input wiring), just m1-recut-check, full `just check` exit 0, git diff --check clean, no conflict markers.\n- Note: one `just check` run failed with a rustdoc doctest \"Disk quota exceeded\" because /tmp is 81% full (other agents' /tmp trees). Rerunning with TMPDIR on another filesystem passed, so this was the host's /tmp, not the code. scripts/test-fuzz-toolchain.py and cargo-fuzz also need a TMPDIR with room.\n\nFinal-revision smoke (recorded in docs/fuzzing.md)\n- Six targets, 15 s bound each, at c8c93e2 (the docs-only 5d7b225 is its child), nightly-2026-08-21 + cargo-fuzz 0.13.1, offline: zero crashes, timeouts or OOM. Runs: canonical 99746, wire 40679, declarations 53966, teapot 4481, oracle 222454, body 84352.\n- Honest limit: the 90 s per-target campaign in docs/fuzzing.md was run at 1ef9575 before the action adapter merged, so it does not cover the five live action reply parsers; a full six-target campaign over the current parsers has NOT been run. The 15 s smoke is a sample, not a proof.\n- The first declarations smoke did find a real defect in my own change: the strict stanza grammar rejected the producer's index-only `[0]` stanza for an array-rooted document. Fixed at 92b2731; the minimized input is a corpus seed and the replay pins its decisions.\n\ncandidate-topology: the cleanup failure did not recur; scripts/test-candidate-topology.py passed in the final just check. Nothing masked.\n\nLeft for the fresh reviewer: review base c6f7be0 -> target 5d7b225 with seal review/diff; the corpus is binary-marked in .gitattributes, read it with xxd or the replay test; check the new action-reply layer and the two schema overlaps; vote fresh (the previous vote was cleared by the retarget)."}	blake3:-LKsrZwi7BWzJn7KyxqTaOck8J1fH5lcr1vTcM0cuY0
1795549222912011	scourge-verifier-preflight	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2a3	{"body":"Review remediation committed at dc172be665e31a6705ac7da970dbc2bdcf994e63 over c6f7be036846646230f4ceeb9f21d7bc7dba72d0. Addressed all five cr-3qg7qb threads: durable transactional conflict ownership across SIGKILL/unknown effects; frozen-recipe-derived ceiling/session plan; stable PassRef locking; global mutable-resource locking across Teapot projects; composed pinned TCP sink plus driven typed-refusal coverage. Validation: focused store 34/34; scourge-core 146/146 nonignored plus all integrations/docs; pinned Teapot 3/3; pinned Investigation evidence 6/6 plus composed bridge 1/1 (7/7); M1 re-cut 7/7; cargo fmt/clippy/diff clean; normal parallel just check passed. Replied all threads, retargeted cr-3qg7qb to exact HEAD/base, requested fresh review; Rite anchor 01M87H53NZME2WM1GVK7RG7G2A. Bone stays doing and claims held pending fresh native reviewer."}	blake3:DhEQwkVibAfTBpHmPeEibrU9slkymW8o-IWZQwy0gbU
1795549333636763	scourge-lead	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2ai	{"body":"CREDIT-GATE HANDOFF: OrcaRouter stopped the permitted OrcaCyber session after reporting another 0.63 USD required. Workspace .maw/workspaces/bn-2ai is preserved; bone remains doing with needs-cyber. Exact committed HEAD and current Seal target: 5d7b225686f7d49c7080e4360b4f22bf0fa61e8e over base c6f7be036846646230f4ceeb9f21d7bc7dba72d0. Dirty files: .seal/reviews/cr-3cu3tb/events.jsonl, crates/scourge-core/src/teapot/hostile.rs, crates/scourge-core/src/teapot/mod.rs, fuzz/src/lib.rs; untracked fuzz/tests/dump.rs. Completed before the gate: the committed 23-stage harness and prior P1 fixes passed fmt, clippy, parser replay/witnesses/toolchain checks, m1-recut and full just check; six 15-second final-code smokes were clean. New dirty work identified three omitted post-envelope passive parsers and extends teapot_output from 23 to 26 stages: version identity, jobs page and pass ceiling. cargo check with hostile-input and cargo test -p scourge-parser-fuzz --test corpus_replay passed after those dirty edits. Not completed: exact decisions and non-vacuity witnesses for the three new stages, conversion or removal of the temporary dump.rs, docs/pins, full corpus/toolchain/mutation checks, fmt/clippy/full just check, final six smokes, commit, review replies/retarget, fresh vote. Safe resume: enter the preserved workspace without cleaning; inspect the five dirty paths first; finish the three stage expectations and adversarial witnesses; rerun all final gates and smokes; commit; retarget cr-3cu3tb from c6f7be0 to the new exact HEAD and request the native reviewer. The current review is stale once dirty source is committed. No source or evidence was discarded, no workspace destroyed, no merge or push."}	blake3:Ui-SPu5uZZNSmCdEYHSXqRmV_Oc33z0i1zuY9VwqyBg
