1795750229377718	scourge-lead	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2p9g	{"description":"The historical verifier collector lane cannot be qualified safely with the current worker boundary: /runtime/referee is worker-writable, host-prepared authority paths and loopback fixture are namespace-incompatible with the network-none worker, and the native supervisor has no evaluator-owned post-Codex stop seam. Add a protected lifecycle boundary before completing bn-1r9u. The host opens the bn-3o5q mode-0700 referee root outside every worker mount and passes only a fixed inherited FD through the exact strace/Podman/crun launch using pass_fds plus a pinned --preserve-fd contract. Add evaluator-only Scourge support that constructs ProtectedRoot from the FD after exact fstat owner/mode/type validation, sets CLOEXEC immediately, never serializes or exposes the host path, and refuses ordinary public/worker use. Extend the pinned native supervisor to authenticate exact Scourge, historical 6d15 Teapot and Investigation pins; run exact demo start before Codex; close the protected FD before spawning Codex; retain the authenticated fixture/engine; and always issue the exact demo stop after Codex on success, timeout, signal and failure. Bind and retain start/stop stdout, exits, fixture/engine identities and final quiescence. Extend the collector/boundary to prove the protected root is absent from mounts, argv, environment and retained worker evidence; Codex and all descendants lack the FD and cannot read/write/chmod/traverse it; exact supervisor -> demo start/fixture -> Codex -> demo stop parentage and order hold; wrong FD, type, owner, mode, number, inherited descriptor, binary pin, start/stop argv, early close, missing cleanup, alternate mount and symlink/inode substitution fail closed. Keep the worker network none, c03 lane separate, and make no provider, rate or production-image claim. Add focused adversarial tests plus real offline native qualification. This prerequisite blocks bn-1r9u only and must not alter the frozen bn-360 dependency set.","kind":"task","labels":["eval","qualification","risk:critical"],"parent":"bn-1r9u","size":"l","title":"Add evaluator-owned protected demo lifecycle to native worker"}	blake3:jD4frQBuxy-R4gWPPd9xBORPTkJs37UmS8iedHpxfkg
